Note on the two blocks: the MIT text above is kept verbatim and unbroken so
that automated license detectors (GitHub's licensee, npm, SPDX scanners) can
recognise it. An earlier version explained the derivation in the middle of the
grant, between the copyright lines and "Permission is hereby granted", and
GitHub reported the license as NOASSERTION — legally MIT, but machine-readably
nothing. Explanation goes after the grant, never inside it.
